                %li
                  %a{:href => "#natural_numbers_object"} Natural numbers object
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#enrichment_over_"}
                    Enrichment over
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Ab
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ab
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab
            denotes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian groups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} objects
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+homomorphisms"} group homomorphisms
            between these as
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphisms
          %p
            The archetypical example of an abelian group is the group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            of integers, and for many purposes it is useful to think of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ab
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab
            equivalently as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+modules"} category of modules
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ab
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mi Mod
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Ab \simeq \mathbb{Z} Mod
                  \\,.
          %p
            The category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ab
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab
            serves as the basic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriching
            category in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homological+algebra"} homological algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab-enriched+categories"} Ab-enriched categories
            play much the same role as
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+categories"} locally small categories
          %p
            In this vein, the analog of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ab
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            – or rather in
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            – is the category of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+category"} stable homotopy category
            or rather refined to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category+of+spectra"} stable (infinity,1)-category of spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherence+law"} coherent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            and the role of the archetypical abelian group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            is the played by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere+spectrum"} sphere spectrum
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕊
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#free_abelian_groups Free abelian groups
          #FreeForgetful.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ab
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+category"} concrete category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo :
                    %mi Ab
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U : Ab \to Set
            %p
              to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              sends a group, regarded as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              equipped with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (+,0)
              of a chosen element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \in A
              and a binary, associative and 0-unital operation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} +
              to its underlying set
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (A, +, 0) \mapsto A
                    \\,.
            %p
              This functor has a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi Set
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ab
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : Set \to Ab
              which sends a set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+abelian+group"} free abelian group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}[S]
              on this set: the group of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+linear+combinations"} formal linear combinations
              of elements in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
          %h3#DirectSumEtc Direct sum, direct product and tensor product
          %p
            We discuss basic properties of binary operations on the category of abelian groups:
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+product"} direct product
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            %em
              %a{:href => "#MonoidalAndBipermutativeStructure"} Monoidal and bimonoidal structure
            we put these structures into a more abstract context.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Ab
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A, B \in Ab
              two
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+product"} direct product
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \times B
              is the abelian group whose elements are pairs
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a, b)
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \in A
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in B
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (0,0)
              and whose addition operation is the componentwise addition
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (a_1, b_1) + (a_2, b_2) = (a_1 + a_2, b_1 + b_2)
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is at the same time
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+the"} the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \oplus B
            %p
              Similarly for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FinSet"} FinSet
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ↪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hookrightarrow
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite set
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                    %mo ≃
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\oplus_{i \in I} A_i \simeq \prod_i A_{i}
                    \\,.
            %p
              But for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \in Set
              a set which is not finite, there is a difference: the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \oplus_{i \in I} A_i
              of an
              = succeed "-indexed" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {A_i}_{i \in I}
              of abelian groups is the sub-group of the direct product on those elements for which only finitely many components are non-0
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                    %mo ↪
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\oplus_{i \in I} A_i \hookrightarrow \prod_i A_i
                    \\,.
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+group"} trivial group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Ab
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \in Ab
              (the group with a single element) is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit"} unit
              for the direct sum: for every abelian group we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ≃
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi A
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A \oplus 0 \simeq 0 \oplus A \simeq A
                    \\,.
          .num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              In view of remark
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FreeForgetful"}
              this means that the direct sum of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi I
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert I \vert}
              copies of the additive group of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
              with themselves is equivalently the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+abelian+group"} free abelian group
              on
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\oplus_{i \in I} \mathbb{Z} \simeq \mathbb{Z}[I]
                    \\,.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              two
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+abelian+groups"} tensor product of abelian groups
              is the group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \otimes B
              with the property that a group homomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \otimes B \to C
              is equivalently a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bilinear+map"} bilinear map
              out of the
              %em set
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ×
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \times B
          %p
            See at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+abelian+groups"} tensor product of abelian groups
            for details.
          .num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit"} unit
              for the tensor product of abelian groups is the additive group of
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A \otimes \mathbb{Z} \simeq \mathbb{Z} \otimes A \simeq A
                    \\,.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+abelian+groups"} tensor product of abelian groups
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributivity+law"} distributes
              over arbitrary
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sums"} direct sums
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A \otimes (\oplus_{i \in I} B_i) \simeq \oplus_{i \in I} A \otimes B_i
                    \\,.
          .num_example
            %h6#example_4 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \in Set
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Ab
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in Ab
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi I
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert I\vert}
              copies of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              with itself is equivalently the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+abelian+groups"} tensor product of abelian groups
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+abelian+group"} free abelian group
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              with
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %mi A
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\oplus_{i \in I} A \simeq (\oplus_{i \in I} \mathbb{Z}) \otimes A
                    \\simeq (\mathbb{Z}[I]) \otimes A
                    \\,.
          %h3#MonoidalAndBipermutativeStructure Symmetric monoidal and bimonoidal structure
          %p
            With the definitions and properties discussed above in
            %em
              %a{:href => "#DirectSumEtc"} Direct sum, etc.
            we have the following
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              The category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ab
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab
              becomes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  under
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Ab
                          %mo ,
                          %mo ⊕
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Ab, \oplus, 0)
              %li
                %p
                  under
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product+of+abelian+groups"} tensor product of abelian groups
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Ab
                          %mo ,
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Ab, \otimes, \mathbb{Z})
            %p Indeed with both structures combined we have
            %ul
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Ab
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Ab, \oplus, \otimes, 0, \mathbb{Z})
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bimonoidal+category"} bimonoidal category
              (and can be made a
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bipermutative+category"} bipermutative category
          %p
            It’s also easy to see that under direct sum or tensor product, Ab can be turned into a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            by equipping it with the appropriate braiding map. For example, under
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊕
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \oplus
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_{A, B}(a, b) = (b, a)
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Ab
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Ab, \otimes, \mathbb{Z})
              is equivalently a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Ab
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Ab, \oplus, 0)
              is equivalently just an abelian group again (since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊕
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \oplus
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ab
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab
          %h3#pointed_objects Pointed objects
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ab
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+unit"} tensor unit
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+objects+in+a+monoidal+category"} pointed objects
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ab
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab
            are the objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+homomorphism"} group homomorphism
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z} \to A
          %h3#closed_monoidal_structure Closed monoidal structure
          %p
            Abelian groups are equivalently
            = succeed "-modules." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mod"}
              category of
              = succeed "-modules" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Mod
                    %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod_R
            is closed monoidal for all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+rings"} commutative rings
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ab
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Mod
                    %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab = Mod_{\mathbb{Z}}
            is also closed monoidal.
          %h3#natural_numbers_object Natural numbers object
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers+object"} natural numbers object
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ab
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ab
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+abelian+group"} free abelian group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}[\mathbb{N}] = \bigoplus_{n \in \mathbb{N}} \mathbb{Z}
            on the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mn 0
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z_0:\mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{Z}[\mathbb{N}]
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mi s
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z_s:\mathbb{Z}[\mathbb{N}] \to \mathbb{Z}[\mathbb{N}]
            such that for all abelian groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and group homomorphisms
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:\mathbb{Z} \to A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g: A \to A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_{f, g}:\mathbb{Z}[\mathbb{N}] \to A
            making the following diagram commute:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℤ
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi z
                                %mn 0
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi ℕ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ←
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi z
                                %mi s
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi ℕ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                            %mi f
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi ϕ
                                %mrow
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mi g
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi ϕ
                                %mrow
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mi g
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo ←
                            %mi g
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathbb{Z} &amp; \stackrel{z_0}{\to} &amp; \mathbb{Z}[\mathbb{N}] &amp; \stackrel{z_s}{\leftarrow} &amp; \mathbb{Z}[\mathbb{N}] \\
                  \&amp; \mathllap{f} \searrow &amp; \downarrow \mathrlap{\phi_{f, g}} &amp; &amp; \downarrow \mathrlap{\phi_{f, g}} \\
                  \&amp; &amp; A &amp; \underset{g}{\leftarrow} &amp; A
                  }
          %p
            Abelian groups are
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}[\mathbb{N}]
            has a function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v:\mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{Z}[\mathbb{N}]
            representing the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basis+of+a+free+module"} basis
            of
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}[\mathbb{N}]
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m \in \mathbb{Z}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m \cdot v(0) = z_0(m)
            and for all
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi m
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
